WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Basra, in the eighth century.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.840
Some pious Muslims feel
luxury is choking their faith.

3
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.010
They turn to renunciation.

4
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.710
Many wear coarse wool, and the
name Sufi may come from that wool.

5
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.830
Centuries later, their path
has orders, lodges and shrines,

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.610
from West Africa to Southeast Asia.

7
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.470
Some critics treat it as
a distinct, even rival,

8
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.020
form of religion.

9
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:30.240
So is Sufism a separate branch of
Islam, or the heart of the same faith?

10
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:34.950
In this mission, you'll trace how early
renunciation grew into great orders with

11
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.720
chains of teachers.

12
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.600
Then you'll compare Sunni
and Shi'a responses,

13
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.730
and weigh up what scholars say.

14
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.070
Your mission: weigh up whether
Sufism is a separate branch of Islam,

15
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.070
or its heart.
